seg-881ec6f8fbe0 = A run writes a result document, a chart and a report. <c1/> also writes the scenario's geometry, or its synthesised signal, in the formats other tools already read: a globe viewer, a desktop map, a geographic information system (GIS), a mission-analysis package or a software-defined-radio (SDR) tool. Nothing here reads a clock or the network, and no export carries a generation timestamp, so the same scenario gives byte-identical files on every run.

