seg-e1dd97c47993 = The first packet is the document packet (<c1/>, <c2/>) with a clock spanning the time grid. Each moving object is a packet whose <c3/> has an ISO { "8601" } (International Organization for Standardization date and time format) UTC (Coordinated Universal Time) <c4/>, <c5/> <c6/>, and <c7/> samples <c8/>: seconds after the epoch, metres in the Geocentric Celestial Reference System (GCRS). CesiumJS takes <c9/> as the International Celestial Reference Frame (ICRF), whose axes the GCRS shares. Fixed sites and footprint centres are constant Earth-fixed <c10/> positions with <c11/> <c12/>. A footprint is an <c13/> with both semi-axes equal to its radius; an untimed track a ground-clamped <c14/>. Each packet's <c15/> states the frame again in words.

