seg-be6362f4c7e7 = One <c1/> with a <c2/> per object class. A moving object is a <c3/> holding a <c4/>: one <c5/> per sample (ISO { "8601" } UTC), then one <c6/> per sample (longitude, latitude, height). Sites are <c7/>s, footprints <c8/>s whose ring is closed and counter-clockwise, untimed tracks <c9/>s. Coordinates are World Geodetic System { "1984" } (WGS { "84" }) longitude and latitude in decimal degrees and height in metres above the WGS { "84" } ellipsoid, written with <c10/> <c11/>. KML reads <c12/> as height above mean sea level; the difference, the geoid undulation, is within about ±{ "110" } m and is not applied. The document's description says so.

