seg-37dc14626a6c = One <c1/>. Positions are <c2/> or <c3/> — longitude first, as RFC { "7946" } requires — in WGS { "84" } degrees, with height in metres above the ellipsoid. A moving object is a <c4/> with a <c5/> property holding one ISO { "8601" } time per position; a track that crosses the { "180" }° meridian is written as a <c6/> cut there, as RFC { "7946" } §{ "3.1.9" } asks (the crossing point is interpolated, and <c7/> then lists the original samples only). Sites are <c8/>s, footprints <c9/>s with a closed counter-clockwise exterior ring (§{ "3.1.6" }), untimed tracks <c10/>s. Every feature has a <c11/> property naming the unit of each numeric member.

