seg-ea28a2bd431c = One file per moving object, since an STK ephemeris describes one vehicle. The header gives <c1/> (equal to the number of data rows), <c2/> (UTC, <c3/>), <c4/> with <c5/>, <c6/>, <c7/> and <c8/>; the rows under <c9/> are seconds after the epoch, position in metres and velocity in metres per second, in the GCRS. A scene with only fixed sites or untimed tracks writes no <c10/> file: a fixed point is an STK Facility, not an ephemeris. An id that is not a plain file-name part (a constellation shell and a satellite, <c11/>) is written with every other character as <c12/>, numbered if two ids then coincide.

