seg-d5e34188aa96 = Beside the <c1/> formats, { "0.36" } added library readers and writers for the standard files mission-analysis tools exchange. They take and return text or bytes and touch no file. Each is a VALIDATED row of the <a1>verification matrix</a1>, against the independent implementation named there:

# text
# c1: kshana::odm
# c2: kshana::ndm_xml
seg-cd8b6f2d43be = <b>CCSDS Orbit Data Messages</b> (<c1/>, with <c2/> for the XML form): OPM, OMM and OCM in keyword-value notation (KVN) and NDM/XML, per CCSDS 502.0-B-3 (OPM and OMM versions { "3.0" } and { "2.0" }, OCM { "3.0" }). Checked both ways against Orekit: Orekit reads Kshana's files and Kshana reads Orekit's. The findings that remain are pinned by tests.

# text
# c1: kshana::adm
# c2: kshana::ndm_xml
seg-00b9fc226c06 = <b>CCSDS Attitude Data Messages</b> (<c1/>, with <c2/>): AEM and APM per CCSDS 504.0-B-2, in KVN and NDM/XML. Checked against Orekit the same way, and the record rotations against Orekit's.

# text
# c1: kshana::spk_writer
seg-b8aa23f78f9e = <b>SPICE SPK</b> (<c1/>): writers and readers of NAIF SPK segments of types { "9" } and { "13" } (with the export of a CCSDS OEM to an SPK kernel) and types { "3" } and { "21" } (Chebyshev polynomials and extended difference lines), checked against the NAIF SPICE toolkit's own readers, down to byte identity. Kshana writes the segments from records it is given: it does not fit Chebyshev coefficients or produce difference lines.

